00:57:09,120 --> 00:57:11,920
So remember present discounted values.

426
00:57:11,920 --> 00:57:15,280
So remember those?

427
00:57:15,280 --> 00:57:17,680
In a world of certainty, every asset will sell for that.

428
00:57:17,680 --> 00:57:20,960
Because any asset that is selling for below its present

429
00:57:20,960 --> 00:57:24,640
discounted value is an arbitrage opportunity to go and buy it.

430
00:57:24,640 --> 00:57:27,200
Anything selling for more than its present discounted value

431
00:57:27,200 --> 00:57:29,560
is an arbitrage opportunity to sell it short.

432
00:57:29,560 --> 00:57:32,640
And so the only stable result is the equal

433
00:57:32,640 --> 00:57:34,960
of present discounted value.

434
00:57:34,960 --> 00:57:37,920
And if we've got risk-neutral agents,

435
00:57:37,920 --> 00:57:40,800
so either everyone's risk-averse or the marginal person

436
00:57:40,800 --> 00:57:43,080
is risk-averse, then actually this

437
00:57:43,080 --> 00:57:45,480
holds under uncertainty.

438
00:57:45,480 --> 00:57:50,160
Then everything sells for its expected present discounted

439
00:57:50,160 --> 00:57:51,240
value.

440
00:57:51,240 --> 00:57:53,680
If we've got either everyone risk-averse

